{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Hom.Defs"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition.block_value_of_hblock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition.block_value_of_hblock","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WedderburnTraceDecomposition.lean#L151-L163","doc":"**The block scaling is strictly more informative than the sum.**\n\nIf the weighted decomposition held for *every* `x` merely by assumption, it\nwould still say nothing about an individual block. Conversely `hblock` pins each\nblock term and the sum follows. Recorded as a one-line consequence so the\nasymmetry is visible in the API rather than only in prose: from `hblock` one\nrecovers the value of each `tr(x π_λ)` individually, which the summed form does\nnot give. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition.trace_eq_sum_weighted_characters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition.trace_eq_sum_weighted_characters","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WedderburnTraceDecomposition.lean#L125-L149","doc":"**THE TARGET, DERIVED.  `tr_M(x) = Σ_λ y_λ · χ_λ(x)`.**\n\nThe hypotheses are exactly the two facts the Wedderburn decomposition supplies:\n\n* `hcomplete` — the central idempotents resolve the identity, `Σ_λ π_λ = 1`;\n* `hblock` — the trace restricted to block `λ` is the block character scaled by\n  the central coefficient, `tr(x · π_λ) = y_λ · χ_λ(x)`.\n\nNeither is the conclusion, and the conclusion follows from them without any\nfurther input. `hblock` is the sentence already in `WedderburnDecomp`'s\ndocstring but absent from its fields; supplying it as a field, and deleting\n`trace_decomp`, would turn `QOU.Hecke.Wedderburn.trace_decomposition` from a\nprojection into a theorem.\n\nNote what is *not* claimed here: that any such `y_λ` and `χ_λ` exist, or that\nthey are unique. Existence is the Wedderburn–Artin content and uniqueness is\nSchur orthogonality (Mathas 1999 §3.43); both remain open in the tree. What is\nsettled is that **the summation identity is not an independent axiom** — it was\nnever the thing that needed assuming. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition.trace_decomposition_of_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition.trace_decomposition_of_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WedderburnTraceDecomposition.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**Naming the block terms.** If each `tr(x · π_λ)` is known to equal some\n`val λ`, the trace is the sum of the `val`s. A repackaging of the previous\ntheorem, and the shape the weighted version instantiates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition.trace_eq_sum_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WedderburnTraceDecomposition.trace_eq_sum_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WedderburnTraceDecomposition.lean#L98-L108","doc":"**Completeness alone gives the unweighted decomposition.**\n\n`Σ_λ π_λ = 1` and additivity of the trace give `tr x = Σ_λ tr(x · π_λ)`. The\n`y_λ` do not appear, and cannot: nothing so far distinguishes the blocks. ","signatureChunk":0}]}